oup person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaneko</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawabata</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Ishii</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Gama</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kusakabe</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The core trisaccharide of &#x003b1;-<sc>l</sc>-arabinofuranan: synthesis of methyl 3,5-di-<italic>O</italic>-&#x003b1;-<sc>l</sc>-arabinofuranosyl-&#x003b1;-<sc>l</sc>-arabinofuranoside</article-title><source>Carbohydr Res</source><year>1995</year><volume>268</volume><fpage>307</fpage><lpage>311</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0008-6215(94)00327-C</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kaneko S, Kawabata Y, Ishii T, Gama Y, Kusakabe I (1995) The core trisaccharide of &#x003b1;-l-arabinofuranan: synthesis of methyl 3,5-di-O-&#x003b1;-l-arabinofuranosyl-&#x003b1;-l-arabinofuranoside. Carbohydr Res 268:307&#x02013;311 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7736473</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaneko</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuno</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsuo</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Ishii</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kobayashi</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayashi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kusakabe</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Substrate specificity of &#x003b1;-<sc>l</sc>-arabinofuranosidase from <italic>Trichoderma reesei</italic></article-title><source>Biosci Biotechnol Biochem</source><year>1998</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>2205</fpage><lpage>2210</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1271/bbb.62.2205</pub-id></citation><